0..74 Comment "// A recursive call whose descending argument is another recursion\'s stuck"
75..151 Comment "// call, beside an argument the arm passes through a definition: unfolded at"
152..226 Comment "// that call, the arm runs the definition before it recurses, and the path"
227..302 Comment "// states the recursion with the definition still written. Both sides apply"
303..378 Comment "// the recursion at the one stuck call and differ only in that argument, so"
379..454 Comment "// they compare part by part, the definition unfolding to meet what the arm"
455..462 Comment "// ran."
464..506 Comment "// The naturals the recursion takes apart."
